  "releases": [
    {
      "version": "1.0.0",
      "channel": "stable",
      "date": "2026-09-29",
      "status": "available",
      "source": {
        "repository": "https://github.com/DreamWeave-MP/dream_archive",
        "tag": "1.0.0",
        "revision": "94f37c74ce288470e3b99b7885937bdd778b8fa8"
      },
      "notes": {
        "summary": "First stable release: the Luau binding is an l3i extension providing @dream/archive, every archive family looks entries up by hash, and lookups and zlib reads allocate less.",
        "migration": "Compose `dream_archive::luau::ArchiveExtension` into the host's l3i `RuntimePlan`. A host that\nstill wants the `dreamArchive` global adds\n`RuntimePolicy::compat_global(\"@dream/archive\", \"dreamArchive\")`.\n[Embedding Luau](https://dreamweave-mp.github.io/dream_archive/docs/luau-hosts/#from-0-2) lists\nwhat scripts must change.\n",
        "added": [
          "`get_by_hash`, `get_id_by_hash` and `contains_hash` on every archive family, `get_id` by path, and `HashFields::from_numeric`.",
          "`archive:readInto(entry, buffer, offset)` in Luau decodes a member straight into a `buffer`, and `archive:getByHash` and `archive:containsHash` take the family's hash shape.",
          "Luau type definitions for the whole module, checked by Luau's own type checker in the tests behind the `luau-analysis` feature.",
          "`toBuffer()` on every Luau builder; only `ba2.Builder` had it.",
          "`dream_archive::flate2`, the re-exported `flate2` whose `Compression` `set_zlib_level` takes, so naming a zlib level needs no `flate2` dependency of your own."
        ],
        "changed": [
          "Path lookups normalize into a stack buffer instead of allocating: `contains` over 4096 distinct paths takes 0.39 ms instead of 1.03 ms (TES3) and 1.43 ms (TES4).",
          "zlib members inflate from the archive through one inflater per thread: a 64 KiB TES4 member reads in 18 µs instead of 68 µs.",
          "Walking entries from Luau is 5 to 23 times faster than with `mlua`, and small calls such as `contains` and `readEntry` take about half as long: 4096 TES3 entries take 0.73 ms instead of 6.15 ms.",
          "dream-path 1.0 and l3i 1.0.0 come from crates.io; Rust 1.92."
        ],
        "fixed": [
          "`Dx10Builder::add_dds_bytes` and `add_dds_file` take DDS files whose depth field is 1, as many tools write for ordinary textures. A DDS file is a volume texture only when its flags have `DDSD_DEPTH` or its caps have `DDSCAPS2_VOLUME`.",
          "A cubemap's extended `DX10` DDS header has an array size of 1, one cube, as the DDS format and DirectXTex count it: extraction wrote 6, which DirectXTex-based tools read as six cubes, and `add_dds_bytes` and `add_dds_file` refused cubemaps saved by texconv. Cubemaps extracted by earlier versions, which say 6 over one cube's data, are still accepted.",
          "Every family matches a lookup path the same way, with dream-path's normalization. BA2 lookups kept repeated separators and dropped a trailing one, so `meshes//door.nif` missed and `meshes/door.nif/` found a member a BSA answered the other way round; hash-only TES4 lookups missed `a//b/c.nif`. Archives without names now hash the normalized path.",
          "Luau `entry.name` is the part of the path after its last separator in every family. For a BA2 entry it was the whole stored path, the same as `entry.path`.",
          "Luau `entry.folder` is `\"\"` for an entry at the root of a TES3 archive or a BA2, as it was for TES4, instead of `nil`; `nil` means the archive stores no names.",
          "The crate builds with only the `ba2` feature: it now enables the `lz4_flex` feature its compressor needs, which only `bsa-tes4` turned on before. Builds with one BSA family alone no longer carry dead code."
        ],
        "breaking": [
          "The `luau` feature (`lua` is the old name of the same feature) binds the crate as an l3i extension, `luau::ArchiveExtension`, providing `@dream/archive`. `dream_archive::lua`, the `mlua` types and the `standalone-lua` feature are gone.",
          "Building with the `luau` feature needs l3i's toolchain: clang, lld and cross-language thin LTO.",
          "Every `open*` in Luau returns the one `Archive` type; `archive:entries()` is a view of entry handles, not a table of tables.",
          "Luau entry hashes are integers: `entry.hash` and `entry.folderHash` replace the old tables and fields, with `hashHex` and `folderHashHex` for the hex spelling. BA2 hashes are `directoryHash`, `fileHash` and `extensionHash`; sizes and offsets are `size`, `storedSize` and `offset` on every format.",
          "Luau integer arguments must be exact: `readEntry(1.5)` is an error instead of a rounded read.",
          "`bsa::Error::InvalidFileRecordFlags` is gone. Nothing returned it: both flag bits of a TES4 file record are read as the format defines them."
        ]
      },
