    {
      "version": "0.1.0",
      "channel": "stable",
      "date": "2026-04-27",
      "status": "available",
      "source": {
        "repository": "https://github.com/DreamWeave-MP/dream_archive",
        "tag": "0.1.0",
        "revision": "0ee5dcba6cdf732d629f3f1bbd1890470375eb58"
      },
      "notes": {
        "summary": "First release: read, extract and write BA2, TES3 BSA and TES4 BSA archives in pure Rust.",
        "added": [
          "`Archive`, which detects the family of any supported archive and lists, reads and extracts it.",
          "BA2 GNRL and DX10 reading and extraction; DX10 textures come out as DDS files with headers rebuilt from the archive's metadata. GNMF archives are identified, not extracted.",
          "TES3 BSA reading, extraction and writing.",
          "TES4 BSA reading, extraction and writing for versions 103, 104 and 105: zlib and LZ4 frames, string tables, embedded names, and hash-only archives through `extract_to_with_paths`.",
          "BA2 GNRL writing, and DX10 writing from DDS files or from texture metadata and raw payloads.",
